Interactive hero Event decisions (reordered runSauronEvents)

The Event Step's "Choose one" is the hero's decision. Previously it was
auto-resolved. Now, when the hero is human, the event effect pauses via
stepResolveTree and the human resolves it through the pendingTree modal.

runSauronEvents is reordered so token placement, plot registration, the
phase transition to SauronMinions, and human-Sauron action setup all run
BEFORE applying the (possibly-pausing) event effect. Since a single event
is resolved per step, the pausing effect runs last and resume is
self-contained -- avoiding the phases<-combat module cycle on resume.

advance() and the App "Advance phase" button now guard on pendingTree.

